  "title": "Feeling, Love and Humankind: path, phil, miso and anthrop",
  "short": "path means feeling, phil means love, miso means hate and anthrop means human being.",
  "trouble": "empathy (feeling with someone) is not sympathy (feeling sorry for someone), and apathy (no feeling) is not antipathy (dislike).",
